# What must not travel into a deployed image.
#
# The Dockerfile is a plain `COPY . .`, and `gcloud run deploy --source .` uploads this working
# directory. Without this file that includes `data/`, the local JSON stores - which after a test
# run hold hundreds of probe tasks, throwaway prompts and test contacts. Those would become the
# deployed instance's starting state, and the demo would open on somebody's test debris.
#
# gcloud does fall back to .gitignore when no .gcloudignore exists, which would have covered
# `data/` by accident. Stating it here makes the upload deterministic instead of dependent on
# that fallback still behaving the same way.

.git/
.gitignore

# Local runtime state: every deployment starts from the seeded corpus, exactly as a fresh
# checkout does (README, "Reset the demo data").
data/

# Local-only working material, none of it needed to run the service.
_reports/
_media_build/
_analysis/

# Marketing/media assets the running app never serves. docs/media holds the local demo-video
# masters (hundreds of MB, gitignored) - and because this .gcloudignore exists, gcloud does NOT
# fall back to .gitignore, so without these lines every `gcloud run deploy --source .` would
# upload them and bake them into the image.
docs/media/
youtube-play-thumb.png

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
*.egg-info/

.venv/
venv/

.env
.env.*
credentials*.json

.vscode/
.idea/
